        "author": "Tournasol7",
        "date": "2018-11-13",
        "license": "CC BY-SA4.0; viewed only",
        "observations": "Actually inspected full dedicated photograph: eroded rough concrete/stone retaining remnants, shallow arched and rectangular recesses with metal grilles, exposed pale stone/masonry facing and horizontal courses, native grassy slope, scattered grey marble fragments, independent Tabularium wall and later church/street stairs behind. No ancient roof or standing colonnade is visible. No pixels copied."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_of_Concord_in_Rome_(2).jpg",
